A thorough end-to-end investigation found no fault anywhere in this topology. Both BGP routers are healthy: router1 (AS 1, 193.10.11.1) and router2 (AS 2, 193.10.11.2) have an established eBGP session that has been up continuously, with one prefix received and two prefixes sent on each side. router1 correctly carries the BGP-learned route 200.1.1.0/24 via 193.10.11.2, and router2 carries 195.11.14.0/24 via 193.10.11.1 — both installed in the FIB. All four interfaces on the two routers are in UP/LOWER_UP state with zero RX/TX errors or drops. The hosts (pc1 at 195.11.14.2 and pc2 at 200.1.1.2) each have the correct address and a default route pointing to their respective gateway. Live bidirectional pings between pc1 and pc2 complete with 0% packet loss and normal latency (~3 ms). No firewall rules or traffic shapers are present on any device. The network is fully operational and the inter-site path is intact. The most likely explanation for the helpdesk ticket is a transient disruption (e.g., a brief BGP session flap during lab startup) that self-resolved before this investigation began. No corrective action is required.
